  Already run your own reverse proxy, such as SWAG, Pangolin, Nginx Proxy
  Manager, Traefik or Caddy? Choosing this changes nothing here. Run self-host
  access export to print where each App lives, then give it to your proxy. You
  stay in charge of names, certificates and who gets in. Home network keeps
  working. This one is for advanced users.

  Who is this for?
  Advanced users who already run a reverse proxy, such as SWAG, Pangolin,
  Nginx Proxy Manager, Traefik or their own Caddy, or want to run one. You
  keep control of names, certificates and who gets in.

